/// Behavioral API documentation for the Roadie Roster backend.
/// Static Markdown authored from the current backend source; reads no state.
mixin () {
  /// Return the backend API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Roadie Roster Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nBackend for **Roadie Roster**, the new-hire tracking app for Bubba's 33 store #975 in Lake Charles, LA (opening Mon Feb 8, 2027). It stores store configuration, positions (stations) with build-to targets, the opening schedule, checklists, retention settings, roadie cards, kiosk sign-up submissions, access grants, the admin-set kiosk PIN, and the phase-2/3 records (orientation check-off, attendance, training groups, trainer notes, leader talks, final sign-offs, alerts).\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nEvery method that reads or writes application data requires a **signed (non-anonymous) caller**. The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available; an agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\n### Registration prerequisite\n\nSigning in is not enough: a principal must be **registered** before any role-guarded call succeeds. Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend and calls `requestAccess()` once. A principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\n- `requestAccess()` records the caller in the pending list and returns `true` when the caller is already registered (or already pending). It is safe to call repeatedly.\n- An unregistered or anonymous caller receives a trap on every guarded endpoint: `Access denied: caller is not registered or access has ended`.\n- A Kiosk login receives `Access denied: Kiosk logins may only submit a sign-up` on every read.\n- An expired access grant (past its access end date) is treated as unregistered.\n\n### Registration evidence\n\n| Row | Caller | Role assigned |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `first_caller_role` | The platform's first authenticated user (the shared authorization owner) | `admin`, via `bootstrapAdmin()` while no app admin exists yet |\n| `later_caller_role` | Any later (non-first) initializer who signs in and calls `requestAccess()` | none yet — the caller is recorded as a **pending** request with no role and stays pending until an Admin approves them with `approveUser()` |\n\n### First-admin bootstrap\n\n`bootstrapAdmin()` bridges the platform's shared authorization grant into the app's access model. It succeeds only while no app admin exists and only for the platform's first user; it returns `true` when the caller holds an app Admin grant after the call. `adminCount()` reports the number of non-expired admins.\n\n## Roles and authorization\n\nRoles: `admin`, `storeManager`, `trainingManager`, `leadership`, `visitingManager`, `trainer`, `kiosk`, `integration`.\n\n- **Admin** — full access; the only role that may manage access grants, store configuration, positions, schedule, checklists, retention, and the kiosk PIN.\n- **Store Manager** — manager-level access: roadie cards with contact sets, sign-up approval, build-to adjustment, trainer notes, exports.\n- **Trainer** — sees only roadies in the stations listed in their grant's `trainerPositionIds`; a trainer with no stations sees no roadies. Trainer notes are restricted the same way.\n- **Integration** — sees only the Shareable export; every roadie card, change-log entry, and trainer-note read returns nothing.\n- **Kiosk** — may only submit a sign-up; every read traps.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- **Timestamps** are signed `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (matching `Time.now()`).\n- **Date-only** values are UTC-midnight nanosecond timestamps; exactly zero means \"not set\". A negative value is a real pre-1970 date and is handled correctly by the age helpers.\n- **Identifiers** (`RoadieId`, `PositionId`, `EventId`, `CrewId`, `SignupId`, `ChangeLogId`, `TrainingGroupId`, `LeaderTalkId`, `AlertId`) are `Nat`.\n- **PhotoRef** and **SignatureRef** are platform file-storage references (blob bytes), not text. Fetch a roadie photo with `getPhoto(id)` and a sign-up photo with `getSignupPhoto(id)`; both return `null` when absent or not visible.\n- **Availability** is a list of `{ day, shift }` cells; `day` is one of `wed..tue` and `shift` is `am` or `pm`.\n- **isMinor** and **birthdayMonthDay** are non-sensitive derived values recomputed on every read from the contact-set date of birth in the store time zone, so a roadie who turns 18 stops being flagged as a minor on the next read. `birthdayMonthDay` is `\"MM-DD\"` or `null`.
- **hireDate** is an optional `Timestamp` (nanoseconds) on every roadie card: the day the roadie submitted their kiosk profile. `approveSignup` sets it from the sign-up's `submittedAt`. Existing roadies migrated from before this field fall back to the matching sign-up's `submittedAt` when it can be found, otherwise to the approval time recorded in `hiredAt`; the migration never leaves it `null`. It is returned by `listRoadies`, `getRoadie`, and `listRosterForPosition` (it is not a contact-set field, so it is not redacted). Render it in the store time zone.\n\n## Store configuration and logos\n\n- `getStoreInfo()` (any read-capable role) returns the full store configuration, including `logo` and `secondaryLogo`, each an optional `PhotoRef` (`null` when unset).\n- `getStoreLogo()` is a **public query with no role gate**: any caller, including Kiosk logins and unregistered or anonymous principals, may call it. It returns `{ logo, secondaryLogo }` — both optional `PhotoRef` values — so the kiosk and sign-in screens can render the store logos without passing `getStoreInfo`\'s role gate. An absent logo is `null`.\n- `updateStoreInfo(info)` (Admin only) replaces the whole store configuration, so it persists both `logo` and `secondaryLogo`; pass the current values to keep a logo unchanged.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- `getMyAccess()` returns the caller's own grant, or `null` until an Admin approves them. The frontend polls it while showing the waiting screen; treat `null` as \"still waiting\", not an error.\n- `listPendingSignups()` returns only `#pending` submissions and never includes photo bytes.\n- `getRosterSummary()` returns per-position `{ positionId, positionName, onHand, buildTo, openSpots }`; on-hand counts each roadie once under their main position only.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `requestAccess()` is idempotent.\n- `approveSignup(id, ...)` traps when the submission has already been decided; a retry after success is rejected rather than creating a second roadie.\n- `approveUser(request)` traps when the principal has no pending request; it removes the pending entry on success.\n- `archiveRoadie` requires a reason; `rehireRoadie` requires a non-blank reason. `updateRoadieStatus` can never set or clear `#archived`.\n- `updateAccessEnd` refuses **any** end date (past or future) on an admin grant, and an Admin grant is always stored with no end date. `updateUserRole` and `removeUser` refuse to leave zero active admins.\n- `adjustBuildTo` applies a signed delta to the stored build-to targets and records a `BuildToAdjustment`.\n\n## Kiosk PIN\n\n- `setKioskPin(pin)` (Admin only) stores only a one-way hash of the PIN; the plaintext is never persisted or returned. An empty PIN traps.\n- `checkKioskPin(pin)` returns `true` when the candidate matches the stored hash; it is a query callable by any caller so the kiosk can gate entry.\n- `hasKioskPin()` returns `true` once an Admin has set a PIN.\n\n## Exports\n\n- `buildShareableExport()` (any read-capable role) returns the export with **no** contact set and **empty** availability arrays, so it never leaks availability.\n- `buildFullExport()` (Admin/Store Manager only) fills the whole contact set, availability by shift and by day, and records a `buildFullExport` change-log entry.\n- Both fill the overview totals: `fohTotalPar`/`bohTotalPar`/`grandTotalPar` and the matching `*Need` fields.\n\n## Errors and traps\n\n- Unregistered or expired callers trap with `Access denied: caller is not registered or access has ended`.\n- Missing role traps name the required role, e.g. `Access denied: Admin role required`.\n- Missing records trap with a message such as `Roadie not found` or `Position not found`.\n- A roadie below a position's minimum age traps on `approveSignup` and `changePosition`.\n\n## Profile fields (About Me)\n\nEvery roadie card and sign-up carries a `RoadieProfile`. The free-text About Me fields are all optional `?Text` and are capped at 200 characters on submission (`submitSignup`): `preferredName`, `hometown`, `hobbies`, `favoriteMovie`, `favoriteSnack`, `favoriteTeam`, `favoriteDrink`, `favoriteColor`, `funFact`, `goalHere`, `positionAppliedFor`. `shirtSize` and `hatSize` are also `?Text` and capped at 200 characters.\n\n- `favoriteTeam`, `favoriteDrink` and `favoriteColor` are the three Gift Bag fields. They were added to `RoadieProfile` by migration `00000006_000000.mo`, which defaults them to `null` for every existing roadie and sign-up so no prior answer is lost. Managers may edit them through `updateRoadieDetails`.\n- `favoriteMovie` is retained on the stored record so existing answers are preserved, even though the kiosk form no longer collects it.\n\n## Gift Bags\n\n- `getGiftBags(filter)` is a **query** returning the Gift Bags shopping list and printable labels. `filter` is `#all`, `#roadies`, `#leaders`, `#foh`, `#boh`, or `#position(PositionId)`. `#all` selects every active (non-archived) roadie plus every leader; `#roadies` selects active roadies only; `#leaders` selects leaders only; `#foh`/`#boh` select roadies by the house of their main position; `#position` selects roadies by main position id.\n- **Leaders** are the manager, trainer and leadership roles (`admin`, `storeManager`, `trainingManager`, `visitingManager`, `trainer`, `leadership`) taken from the access grants. A leader's label carries their title in `positionName` (falling back to a role label), their name, and their About Me answers; leaders have no roadie id (it is `0`) and no house (it is `#foh`).\n- **Authorization:** Admin, Store Manager and Training Manager only. Every other caller — including Kiosk, Trainer, Leadership, Visiting Manager, Integration, unregistered and anonymous principals — is rejected with `Access denied: Admin, Store Manager or Training Manager role required`.\n- The payload never includes phone, email, date of birth or any other contact-set field.\n- `groups` holds one `GiftBagGroup` per category (`#candySnack`, `#drink`, `#sportsTeam`, `#color`, `#shirtSize`, `#hatSize`). Each group's `answers` are grouped **case-insensitively, ignoring extra spaces and punctuation** (for example `snickers`, `Snickers!` and `  SNICKERS ` are one group), the `answer` shown is the most common spelling in the group, and the list is sorted by `count` highest first. `noAnswer` counts selected roadies who left that category blank or unanswered.\n- `labels` holds one `GiftBagLabel` per selected roadie: `roadieId`, `name`, `positionName`, `house`, and the six answers (`candySnack`, `drink`, `sportsTeam`, `color`, `shirtSize`, `hatSize`), each optional. Labels carry no contact information.\n\n## Export columns\n\nBoth the Full and Shareable exports include the four Gift Bag columns `favoriteTeam`, `favoriteSnack`, `favoriteDrink` and `favoriteColor` on every `ExportRow`, populated from the roadie's profile. They are not contact information, so the Shareable export includes them too. The Full export additionally fills the contact-set columns (phone, email, emergency contact, date of birth, availability).\n\n## Staff profiles\n\nA signed-in user may supply a **staff profile** describing who they are. It is stored on their pending request before approval and carried onto their access grant at approval.\n\n- `submitStaffProfile(profile)` (any signed-in caller with a pending request) stores the caller's profile on their pending request. It traps with `No pending request for this principal` when the caller has no pending request (for example an already-approved user). Calling it again replaces the stored profile.\n- `updateMyStaffProfile(profile)` (any signed-in caller with an access grant) updates the caller's own profile on their grant. It traps with `Access grant not found` when the caller has no grant. Existing users approved before profiles existed use this to fill theirs in without losing access.\n- `approveUser(request)` carries `request.staffProfile` onto the new grant; pass the pending request's profile to preserve it.\n- A `StaffProfile` carries `fullName`, `requestedRole`, `title`, `homeStoreNumber`, `homeStoreCity` (all required), and optional `preferredName`, `workPhone`, `workEmail`, `photo`, `trainerPositionIds`, `arrivalDate`, `departureDate`. `arrivalDate`/`departureDate` are `DateOnly` (UTC-midnight nanoseconds); `photo` is an optional `PhotoRef`.\n- The optional About Me fields `hometown`, `hobbies`, `favoriteTeam`, `favoriteSnack`, `favoriteDrink`, `favoriteColor`, `funFact`, `goalHere`, `shirtSize` and `hatSize` were added to `StaffProfile` by migration `00000008_000000.mo`, which defaults them to `null` for every existing grant and pending request. A blank field is stored as absent (`null`).\n- Work phone and email are contact information: only Admin and Store Manager may read them, matching the roadie contact-set rule. `listLeaders` clears both before returning a leader's profile.\n\n## Leaders\n\n- `listLeaders()` is a **query** returning one `LeaderSummary` per leader: `principal`, `role`, `title`, `staffProfile`, `trainerPositionIds`, `arrivalDate` and `departureDate`. Leaders are the manager, trainer and leadership roles (`admin`, `storeManager`, `trainingManager`, `visitingManager`, `trainer`, `leadership`).\n- **Authorization:** readable by every registered role except Kiosk and Integration. Kiosk is rejected with `Access denied: Kiosk logins may only submit a sign-up`; Integration is rejected with `Access denied: Integration role may only read the Shareable export`; unregistered and anonymous principals are rejected with `Access denied: caller is not registered or access has ended`.\n- `title` is the leader's staff-profile title, falling back to a role label (`Admin`, `Store Manager`, `Training Manager`, `Visiting Manager`, `NSO Trainer`, `Leadership`) when the profile is absent or its title is blank.\n- The returned `staffProfile` has `workPhone` and `workEmail` cleared, so no contact information ever leaves the backend. Leaders never count toward on-hand or build-to and never appear in the position roster.\n\n## Store templates\n\n- `downloadStoreTemplate()` (Admin only) returns a `StoreTemplateFile` built from the current positions, schedule, checklists and leader-talk settings. Schedule events are expressed as whole days relative to the store's opening date (`startOffsetDays`, optional `endOffsetDays`; negative = before opening). The file carries a `version` number and deliberately no people data, logos, store number, city or opening date.\n- `loadStoreTemplate(file)` (Admin only) validates and applies a template. It returns `#err(text)` when any roadie exists (`Cannot load a template once roadies exist`); otherwise it replaces positions, schedule and checklists, recomputes every schedule date from this store's opening date, updates the leader-talk name and sizes, and returns `#ok(preview)` with the applied counts. Position and event ids are reassigned sequentially from zero.\n- `saveStoreTemplate(name)` (Admin only) snapshots the current configuration under a name in the in-canister template store; it is separate from the downloadable file.\n\n## Mutation retry safety (continued)\n\n- `submitStaffProfile` and `updateMyStaffProfile` are idempotent replacements: re-sending the same profile is safe.\n- `loadStoreTemplate` is destructive: it clears and replaces positions, schedule and checklists. Re-running it with the same file is safe (it refuses once roadies exist, and otherwise reproduces the same state).\n";
  };
};
